INT. SALT MINE - CORPORATE RETREAT HALL - DAY

A vaulted chamber a thousand feet underground, carved from white crystal. String lights. Folding tables. A flip chart reads "OUR CULTURE: DEPTH."

FELICITY ARMSTRONG-NWOSU, 40s, a regional director in a hard hat and blazer, stands in front of the flip chart with a marker. At the table sits GIDEON PALAMARCHUK-DIOP, 30s, an analyst, glaring at the screen of a phone that has no signal.

She taps the chart.

FELICITY
Depth. Roots. Foundation. Let's build this from the ground down.

GIDEON
We are literally underground.

FELICITY
Exactly.

He sighs. She writes "TRUST" in the margin and underlines it twice.

FELICITY (CONT'D)
Trust.

He looks at the phone. Looks at her. Puts the phone away.

GIDEON
Okay. I trust you.

FELICITY
Do you?

GIDEON
No.

FELICITY
Good. That's honest.

She sets down the marker. The mine hums with ventilation.

The elevator door dings. A third person steps off, brisk and bright-eyed: ANNELIESE VON TRAPP-OKAFOR, 50s, a consultant in a white lab coat, carrying a wooden box.

ANNELIESE
I'm sorry I'm late. The cage was slow.

FELICITY
Anneliese! We were just on trust.

ANNELIESE
Wonderful. I brought the exercise.

She sets the box on the table. Opens it. Inside, eight small salt crystals, glittering.

ANNELIESE (CONT'D)
Each of you will pick one. Hold it. Tell me what it means.

Gideon holds one up. Peers at it. Felicity takes another, hesitates, turns it over.

GIDEON
It means my hands are cold.

ANNELIESE
Gideon.

GIDEON
It means I miss the sun.

ANNELIESE
That's a start.

FELICITY
(softly)
It means I have not seen my kids in a week.

Silence. Gideon looks at her. She stares at the crystal, not at him.

ANNELIESE
(gently)
That's the exercise.

FELICITY
Is it?

ANNELIESE
Yes.

Felicity blinks hard. Gideon pulls a chair beside her. He doesn't say anything. After a moment, she sets the crystal down.

FELICITY
Let's go up.

GIDEON
The elevator doesn't run until four.

FELICITY
Then we'll wait.

They sit. Anneliese packs the box. The lights hum.
